1
00:03:20,869 --> 00:03:26,869
Naughty girls go to hell... Really naughty girls conquer it.

2
00:06:41,739 --> 00:06:47,739
Lady Death is a fantasy, animation, horror film directed by Andy Orjuela.

3
00:10:02,608 --> 00:10:08,608
When accused by the townspeople of being in league with the Devil,
Hope finds herself in a satanic deal for her life.

4
00:13:23,478 --> 00:13:29,478
After refusing the terms of the deal, she transforms into the powerful Lady
Death and vows to wrest control of hell from her father.

5
00:16:44,347 --> 00:16:50,347
Lady Death / Hope (voice), played by Christine McPeters Auten.

6
00:20:05,217 --> 00:20:11,217
Lucifer / Matthias (voice), played by Mike Kleinhenz.

7
00:23:26,086 --> 00:23:32,086
Pagan (voice), played by Andy McAvin.

8
00:26:46,956 --> 00:26:52,956
Cremator (voice), played by Rob Mungle.

9
00:30:07,826 --> 00:30:13,826
Asmodeus / Large Torture Troll (voice), played by Mike MacRae.

10
00:33:28,695 --> 00:33:34,695
Niccolo (voice), played by Chris Patton.

11
00:36:49,565 --> 00:36:55,565
Lady Death is a fictional goddess appearing in American
comic books published by Coffin Comics.

12
00:40:10,434 --> 00:40:16,434
Created by Brian Pulido, Lady Death first appeared in
Eternity Comics' Evil Ernie #1 in December 1991.

13
00:43:31,304 --> 00:43:37,304
Lady Death then reappeared in the Evil Ernie: The Resurrection miniseries
published by Pulido under his now-defunct company Chaos!

14
00:46:52,173 --> 00:46:58,173
Comics in 1994.

15
00:50:13,043 --> 00:50:19,043
The character was also the subject of a full-length animated
feature film released in July 2004 by ADV Films.

16
00:53:33,913 --> 00:53:39,913
Incarnations of the character have been illustrated by such comic book artists as
Steven Hughes, Mike Deodato, Romano Molenaar, Dheeraj Verma and Ivan Reis.

17
00:56:54,782 --> 00:57:00,782
Brian Pulido has optioned publishing licenses through various
independent companies such as CrossGen Comics and Avatar Press.

18
01:00:15,652 --> 01:00:21,652
As of 2024, Lady Death was published by Pulido's Coffin Comics.

19
01:03:36,521 --> 01:03:42,521
By 2017, the comic had sold 15 million copies in seven languages.

20
01:06:57,391 --> 01:07:03,391
In addition, Lady Death has been depicted in artworks by a number of well-known fantasy artists
such as Dorian Cleavenger, Gerald Brom, Boris Vallejo, Joe Jusko and Julie Bell.

21
01:10:18,260 --> 01:10:24,260
The film explores themes of satan, breast, lucifer, demon, adult animation.

22
01:13:39,130 --> 01:13:45,130
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
